  return discoveryFailed(candidateSeen?nbdisplaywait::CandidateLayoutRejected:nbdisplaywait::NoDisplayClassMatch);
 #else
  return discoveryFailed(nbdisplaywait::UnsupportedArchitecture,true);
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f1e3275..02a24b6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -283,3 +283,11 @@ native allocation. Imported resources retain their owner and release ordering.
 Pipeline object collection processes only objects whose last holder was released
 since the preceding collection, using the upstream runtime release queue. It
 retains the exact object keys, destruction order and live shader/layout holds.
+
+The display wait reader accepts only the two verified primary server classes
+and the exact IOMFBDisplay or AppleWirelessDisplay identity in QuartzCore
+76ce2a6e. The latter's original destructor reaches the IOMFBDisplay base without
+adjusting this; the reader accesses no fields of the derived display. Discovery
+checks at most sixteen returned display objects and prefers the exact base
+identity. It retains the selected class in decoded evidence, so an observed
+wireless display is not represented as a physical panel.
